gametitle=Jak 3 (NTSC-U) [SCUS-97330]

// Frame-rate caps for Jak 3, found in RAM from a savestate of the SCUS-97330 (CRC 644CFD03) disc.
//
// Addressing: the kernel global at 0x001297A8 holds the symbol table base (symbol_table+5).
// display-sync's value slot is that + 0xE2BF; its value is the function's code. Each patch is a
// PCSX2 pointer code, so it skips itself until the game has loaded display-sync (slot still 0).
//
// display-sync already holds a frame until it has taken as long as the last one (dog-ratio), then
// reports the time that passed to the game's clocks - except that after waiting it reports 1.0.
// The caps fix the wait target at T vsyncs and keep the measured time, so game speed stays right:
//   +0x108  lui 1.0 -> T   (fmax 1.0 dog-ratio)      floor of the wait target
//   +0x110  lui 4.0 -> T   (fmin 4.0 dog-ratio)      ceiling: target is exactly T, no ratchet after a slow frame
//   +0x204  lui 1.0 -> T   (< 1.0 ratio)             frames already slower than T are not held
//   +0x284  c.eq.s f30,f0 -> c.olt.s f30,f26         hold any frame shorter than T, not only exact-1.0 ones
//   +0x314  mtc1 v1,f30 -> nop                       keep the measured ratio instead of 1.0 after waiting
// Use one cap at a time. Switching one off needs a reboot (the code stays patched until then).

[Perf - 30 FPS Cap]
author=jak-series perf pack
description=Caps the game at ~30 fps through the engine's own frame pacer: every frame is held until 2.0 vsyncs have passed, and the game's clocks advance by the measured time, so game speed stays correct. Use one cap at a time; switching it off needs a reboot.
